\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces A specified correction range in $\symbb R^2$. For $L(a,b)=(a,0)$, the image is the horizontal axis. The defect $(2,3)$ splits into $(2,0)$ in that image and the remaining representative $(0,3)$. Subtracting the image component leaves the same cokernel class. The functional $(x,y)\mapsto y$ vanishes on the correction range and detects the value three. The correction equation $Lu=-(2,3)$ therefore has no solution.}}{46}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:correction-cokernel-example}{{5}{46}{A specified correction range in $\mathbb R^2$. For $L(a,b)=(a,0)$, the image is the horizontal axis. The defect $(2,3)$ splits into $(2,0)$ in that image and the remaining representative $(0,3)$. Subtracting the image component leaves the same cokernel class. The functional $(x,y)\mapsto y$ vanishes on the correction range and detects the value three. The correction equation $Lu=-(2,3)$ therefore has no solution}{figure.caption.5}{}}
